          "type": "turn",
          "question": "And is it ever a sign of something worse?",
          "answer": "**Urgency: routine, based on the description.** The symptom check found no emergency pattern for \"heartburn most evenings.\" That is not a clearance.\n\n**Call emergency services now** if heartburn-type discomfort comes with chest pain or pressure, pain spreading to the arm, neck, or jaw, breathlessness, sweating, or nausea, or if it occurs on exertion. The GERD summary (condition-gerd) says heartburn and cardiac pain cannot be reliably told apart by how they feel, so chest discomfort should not be assumed to be reflux.\n\n**Serious causes the material mentions:**\n- **Heart disease:** the most important one to rule out, as above.\n- **Conditions of the food pipe or stomach:** the GERD guideline (guideline-gerd-initial-management-and-alarm-features) lists alarm features that change the approach, including new symptoms at an older age and a family history of upper gastrointestinal cancer. Those features lead to referral for a camera test (endoscopy) rather than starting with a trial of medicine. The guideline also notes that some people with ongoing symptoms have a different cause, such as a movement problem of the food pipe, which more acid-reducing treatment does not help.\n\n**Seek prompt medical care (not necessarily emergency) for:**\n- Difficulty or pain when swallowing, especially if new or worsening\n- Vomiting blood, or black, tarry stools\n- Unintentional weight loss\n\n**Not in the retrieved material:** I did not find a passage listing the full range of serious conditions linked to heartburn. This answer covers only what the retrieved passages describe.\n\nA doctor can check the pattern against your age, risk factors, and history. Please book an appointment, and seek care sooner if any of the features above appear.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n\n[sources: condition-gerd, guideline-gerd-initial-management-and-alarm-features, red-flag-chest-pain]",
